00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.349
upright double bass, and if you listen

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:51.510
carefully with the perfect pitch that we

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.000
all have, that super low bass note there

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.190
is a C, which is the lowest possible

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.379
pitch of any stringed instrument. Like,

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:00.269
normally the low note on a bass is tuned

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:02.879
to an E, but if you release that string

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:04.829
and make it looser, it can extend lower -

00:03:04.829 --> 00:03:07.379
to a C. "This up here is called an

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:13.000
extension, which allows the bass to go down to a low C.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.280
So, why does Jarate do this?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.959
Well, for one - this is a super low

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:17.849
note and it definitely produces a sense

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:20.099
